  "verbalization": "Azadiradionolide is shown to interact with SNU-387, a compound that is a target of multiple entities, including Azadiradionolide, Neridienone A, and another compound. All these entities ultimately target MOVP-3, suggesting a shared mechanism of action involving the modulation of a common target. The evidence indicates that Azadiradionolide may act through a pathway that leads to the inhibition or regulation of MOVP-3, possibly through a direct or indirect interaction with the target. The presence of multiple distinct molecular structures that share the same target MOVP-3 suggests that the mechanism of action may involve the modulation of a biological process that is conserved across these compounds. The final score of 0.5277 across the three paths supports a plausible relationship, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and the role of MOVP-3 in this process.",
